> API and interpretation

A floating-point quotient can round exactly to an eigenvalue before the residual
reaches the requested tolerance. If the next shifted matrix is exactly singular
while the direction is still unconverged, this API reports a domain error. It
does not regularize that solve or label the unfinished direction converged.

The original Q entries were rounded to four decimal places, so its nominal1,3,7
diagonal is not an exact spectrum certificate. The actual checked QR spectrum is
reported separately. The figure now plots explicitly transformed log10
residuals; the old report claimed a log scale while plotting raw residuals.
Every trace state is a real initial or completed-solve boundary and carries a
matching quotient/vector. Histories stop at real convergence without padding.
The existing unchanged regression failed25 baseline trials in batch304–313; this
native conversion replaces its fragile squared-norm normalization/regularization
path with the canonical robust inverse kernel and adds full regression coverage.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

